\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.2}{\ignorespaces Bifurcation angle on a made-up left main bifurcation, computed with the thesis code. (A) The lumen in grey with its centerline; points are placed every 0.5\,mm between 5 and 10\,mm from the bifurcation point $O$, measured along the centerline. (B) Close-up of the dotted region: a line is fitted through each set of points (dashed back towards $O$), and $\theta $ is the angle between their directions $\mathbf  {u}_{\mathrm  {LAD}}$ and $\mathbf  {u}_{\mathrm  {LCx}}$.\relax }}{32}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:method-angle}{{6.2}{32}{Bifurcation angle on a made-up left main bifurcation, computed with the thesis code. (A) The lumen in grey with its centerline; points are placed every 0.5\,mm between 5 and 10\,mm from the bifurcation point $O$, measured along the centerline. (B) Close-up of the dotted region: a line is fitted through each set of points (dashed back towards $O$), and $\theta $ is the angle between their directions $\mathbf {u}_{\mathrm {LAD}}$ and $\mathbf {u}_{\mathrm {LCx}}$.\relax }{figure.caption.14}{}}
\newlabel{fig:method-angle@cref}{{[figure][2][6]6.2}{[1][31][]32}}
